        <p>The excess of births aver deaths was 19. The Birth ROA was equal to 26 per 1,000 of the population. The death-rate from all causes was equal to 10 5 per 1.000, against 181 the average of the previous 4 weeks, and against 16 5 the corresponding period of last year. The death- rate from th, seven chief zymotie diseases was equal to 1 6 per 1.000, against 4.6 the average rate of the previous 4 weil4, and against 1-6 the corresponding period of 1898. The a;ies of mortality were- -0-1 1-5 5-15 15-25 25-65 65 up. 3 1 2 2 13 The deaths ineityled-2 from measles, 4 from lung diseases. 7 from all other cause. Toe following e.ses of Infectious Disease have been reported during the week :—Scarlet fever 8 cases, en. eric fever 1 rase, erysipelas 1 case. Total number of patients in hospital week ending 20th May, 48 METEonoLoov—The mean temperature was 521 Fah., 2.ncl therefor' 3-1 clegrres higher than the preceding week. The maximum temperature 66F., was recorded on the 18-,n inst., and the minimum temperature 41F., on the 19 h inst. - --</p>
        <p>Th Ramfali measured -55 inch. Tho general direc- tion was S.W.</p>
