        <p>At the Police Court yesteruay Satnuel Hill was charged with attempting to ccmtnit suicide on till 4th May.— The Chief Const‘ila e sail defend...et was a single man and had been for a few months in Warriegton. He waa a beestead maker, from Striniughael, hut was working at his tree° in Warrinet in. Eh, 1 idged with Mr Coeeer at 159, Orford-laue, and abut twenty minutes to two on the afternoon in qiiestion, defetioatit was aloe° in the buta,e with the exception of a girt of. abitat 14 years. eent her nut for bier and when he cme back the door was locked. She saw the isiioner through the window and raised an alarm. Tne door was burst leen and d f indant was found with his throat cat. He was taken to the Infirrniry where he had riace been tying betweea lite and death He (the Chief Constable) had a conversation with the house surgeon at the lefirmary who said the man seemed hardly tit cot to be free. He wou!cl withdraw the chari,e against tee man who might be rlmnied to the Workhouse where his condition could he inquin-d into.—A r. mtrid was granted for a fortni,zr t 3-EIVEKILE THIEVES —A MAGISTRATE'S STRONG RENAMES. Ac tee War,in4con LI ireuela P .lice C atm oi S teroay before Mr. Cuandley tne coal-), and n.he- magis- tra•l-s. James C. Tine (12), George }tarsier (10,, an 4 Thotnaa Curry (10% were tat oueht up on renal frena Friday chkrged with stealieg 'rem the Marker. Piaui be- twain Thursday night and F.ed y in 'ruing a sack is. 31. the propeity of Williern Whiitaker. Thor were further chareel wich -ailing in in a treble off L egh- street on Mt 24 te lust, a due-coleure I mare tog..t-ier with s bride the property of Meatirs. Magien ilr.o, he value of £l2 43; with stealing from a temporerily inneecupiee house, 10. Ha overee•reet, on the 23rd iast., 1/ breast pins, a gold ring, diver mela!, and silverl bax, a Itnifi and tour p of stockings, the property of Jane Ashworth.—The prisoners. whose heals just tipped the dock, pie d d guilty.—From the evidence it appe