        <p>The annul( meeting of the Ru -morn Rogb 7 Foo.b til Club W 43 bell at Mr. Riley's Ca'6, 13,idge-screot, Rni• corn, on Toes lay nsl.4hr, wh.n -.hire were aboot 120 memners present. Ett tle on a.t the S,crstary ia.,im'Lea that tleir pre udern Cdr PSJ ,411 flan. 0 C ) was pre- vented thiou4h illnoss from at•-nlin.4 th meting. Mr. W Carroll was eleeeiti to the chair, and on tak- ing his sea said he was sorer to b t at) Algise for Mr. P. Soetkrn tn. Toes/ ha I trt.v 11-id 1-ng rh eo at- tend a ne-t,iig ,“ the C cia .o n. nu M. SJe ;km tn hid apo.area so unwed tha he (toe Coairma i) had per • t,ua lel him to go home. M. Sp'akmao epresalhi anxi-ty to be pres at trid A %Trail., d•al of c fie could assure them that Vb. Spe kkma ha i only goni home on his pile. C pMtUttfl. Liter Mr. Carrot said tha a.lt-tru4h Mr. Sp.ak nit w.s un khie o he present he ha i told him co see th it they got their cut- tomary cigar. (liar. hP tr )</p>
        <p>TEE SECRETARY'S REPORT. The Secretary (Mr J. E i cie), e,d tois report as fol- lows :—ln presenting to yeti the record of the past season, it is gratif vine to he a.b!e to repoit a decide-Hy more favourable etevee if ,ffa re than that which viol chronicled twelve menthe ; eed +hi • to, in spite of new obstacles weieletave hat co be encou itered. With the introduction ot legaisee pr)fesei .n dism, those who are fully anquainted wih tee poeiti in the Rencern fltuo occupied in rela .ion too her clubs in the Northern Cam), can b ast aepr date tl4 situation Oar Mender res iurces as re,ger is fieanciei sepp .r m-k i; a met .erl of the err aeest aitfieultv to compete under profe•sione rules, wt i th se ore ,ros watch happ an to be co for. un ,tely situated in 'neee c titres of p ipuletion, teat they ean c, in nand a large following, .eou:e the b !st gate, ad off .r the mist temp.:We indu.lem ants to Wflet.l oin n ative talent can co neete eiicerses- fully again.t sum' powerful and intiential organize ions (and here, of course, we have in our naiads ee the bril- lent vie ory over Oldham on March 4 h), it is an achievement ot whieh the town has good ca-eie to be proud, and which renects the highest possible credit oe our players. The record of the past season, with which we precer-d to deal, will, we confidently h ape, ju•tify the for 'going obseiv alone). During the pia season several desirable im• protementi were effected ; the dreising room Wl4 repaired and put ie better order, wiiiiat thi proprietors Messrs. Greeneil Whitley and Come iny erected a large bath and we can no v b Jest of being in posses •i ‘n of one of the finest bath; possessed by any club in the Northern Union. The fi 1 was considerably improved by nevi ig a large portion ot the playing eec,osure relaid. Sports were again held and there was every indication of a very chime sful meeting being h .Id but unfertuitately the weather was of an untavnurab'es description Luckily, however, we came out on