        <p>f 1)4%re1l Backache lidnii—Plll3 will be given away free to every person sof( .ring with k 'way ailme ,t who will call at the unthrsigned address. First cune, first served, and only this one chance offe ed. R Inemb-r this is not a sample box, but a regular size box ot Doao's Backache Kidnay Pills, which retails at two shillings aud nine - pence.</p>
        <p>Remember, FR lIR DISTRIBUTION 1 DAY ONLY, JUNE 6th at B3ots Gash Crum s;,a, 6, Oemsk,e, Sc. Helens.</p>
        <p>MAY QUEEN Fx.,..SEIV A. 14 AT HAYDOCK.</p>
        <p>This festival, which, in cons.vence of the rain, had to be pottponed from the 13 I; May, WAS bretlplt to a successtul conclusion on Saturday. The day was beauti- fully nee sad there Was cmseq to ally a large turnout. Every preparation had been mule to ensure a brilliant pageant,and to some extent the cAninittee's • &amp;its were succesaful. Large crowds of people from the various neighbouring villages attended, arad lined the route of the procession, whiala after being formed on the Hay- dock Football Club, proceeded to Penny-lane, back again to the Ship lan at Blackorook, returning to tee field ter the Coronation -lieremony. The procession was made up in the following order:— Haydock Brass Band. Floral Dancers, Cricketers. The White Slave, Bailors, Flower Girls, - Footballers, Spring, Summer. Autumn. &amp; Winter, Day &amp; Night. Lawn Tennis. Gipsy Girls, Prince, Bed Riding Hood, Bakers. Boating Girls, Volunteers, Nancy Lees, White Sailors. Grace Darllag, News Boys, Dressmakers, Blue Sailors. Fairies, Australia, Teachers. Lawn Tennis Plovers. Vclunteer, ax Queen's Carriage, Regular, Flower LS-iris (ha c)nveyance), Soldiers, Lady Hunter. Albania, Clown and Pantaloon, A.I. Bobby. Boating, Brass Band, May Pole Dancers, Jockey, Sleeping Beauty, Irish Lad. Hospital Nurses, Collie • $ and Joiners, Milkmaids, Zulu, Britannia, Nations, Gipsy Lads, Physical Rxercise Performers, Servants. John Bull, Armed° .n Girls, Canada, Italian &amp; Swiss Girls, Archbishop, Sword Bearer, Sceptre Be tree, Crown Bearer, The May Queen in her Carriage. attended by Military Bsoort, Scotch Highlanders. Train Bearers, Maids of Honour and Pages, Marines with Gun on Carriage, Niggers, This year's Queen was Yliis Len, and she hoked ex ceedingly becoming in nor dtess of white. Tae corona- tion was performed by Miss Maggie Lee. There were sev,ral [yr formancea on the field, cmsist- ing ot a Triple Bar perf mance by Jake, Atfred and Myra Lo-La, and an ealaibijin by F &amp;wise° the export lamp manipulator. Ti:e May-pole dancers exectred tieir evolutions in a remarkably clever manner, reflecting credit on Mr. J. Ralpho by whom they were trained. The manual exercise by Scotch Highlanders under the supervision of Lance Sergeant J. Kynastm wis well carried out, and the physical drill by children from Blackbroek Infant Schools, trained by Miss Sawyer, was interesting. The chtldren afterwards left the field,which was given up to dancing.</p>
      </div>
